\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Intervenes \highlight\uc2  More Despite Lower USD Inflow\b0\par\par\uc2 1,241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 00:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 6:24 (Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts this week with no clear trigger for the actions, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  says. Late Monday the bank announced an auction to roll over the $2B reverse swap due April 2, again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market Wednesday with a dollar purchase estimated at $800M to $1.1B, possibly the biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market so far this year, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  says. Moreover, a fall-off in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows seems at odds with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive stance to curb the real's appreciation, with inflows sinking to $500M the week before last compared to a weekly $1.5B average, although still robust for the year to date, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  says. (diana.kinch@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 6:16 (Dow Jones) The much feared plunge in European tech spending isn't showing itself as far as Tibco Software (TIBX) CEO Vivek Ranadive is concerned. Fiscal 1Q European sales rose 46% over a year ago and five of the 10 largest deals signed in the quarter were struck with European customers. "You guys kept telling us that it would blow up in Europe," he said during the analysts call. The company intensified its focus there and he remains encouraged by demand there. TIBX is down 1.2% at $32.05 in after-hours trading. (steve-d.jones@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 6:13 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  is keeping the ratings on Residential Capital, the struggling mortgage subsidiary of \uc2 Ally Financial\uc2  (GMA.XX), unchanged after a Mexican subsidiary failed to get enough participation in a proposed debt exchange. Had the exchange gone through, S&P may have lowered ResCap's rating to "selective default" because the transaction would have amounted to a distressed exchange. ResCap is currently on CreditWatch with negative implications as two senior credit facilities that Ally provides it come due April 13. Ally has said further financial support for ResCap is not guaranteed. (andrew.r.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 6:08 (Dow Jones) Baby boomers will like Canada's budget more than civil servants, says National Bank Financial. The FY2012-13 budget will result in the elimination of 12,000 government positions over a three-year-period. Taking into account attrition through retirements and voluntary departures, federal employment will be reduced by 19,200, or 4.8%, NBF says. The decision to change eligibility for the old age supplement to 67 from 65 starting in 2023 will have a limited impact on the bulk of baby boomers, NBF says. "While it is a step in the right direction, it could have been implemented earlier," the bank adds. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 5:58 (Dow Jones) RIMM CEO doesn't completely shut door on possible takeover in response to analyst question. Thorsten Heins reiterates strategic review is focused on managing company turnaround, but if "there was an element that we detected during the strategic review that would lead us into (the) direction" of a possible sale "we would consider it." RIMM down 2.8% to $13.33 after hours. (ben.dummett@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 5:56 (Dow Jones) Canada's Finance Minister Jim Flaherty, who didn't introduce any new measures in the budget to cool a hot housing market "knows when to tap the brakes" Frank Techar, \uc2 Bank of Montreal\uc2 's head of Canadian banking, tells Dow Jones. "Banks have all the tools they need to help customers borrow smartly," he says. \uc2 BMO\uc2  had sparked a price war among the banks with its low rate 2.99% mortgages. Techar says about four in 10 new insured mortgages at \uc2 BMO\uc2  have amortizations of 25 years or less, which helps homeowners build equity faster. (caroline.vanhasselt@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 5:49 (Dow Jones) The Chilean economy isn't slowing as quickly as expected, Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said after the release of robust economic data for February. "It's good news but let's be careful as the international outlook is complicated," he said. With industrial and mining output surging and retail sales growing sharply, analysts see economic activity gaining 6%-7% on the year in February. GDP is expected to grow around 4% this year after a 6% gain in 2011. (carolina.pica@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 5:46 (Dow Jones) \uc2 St. Jude Medical\uc2  (STJ) has pulled its Brio Deep Brain Stimulation system for Parkinson's disease off the European market, a move that should be immaterial to STJ's 1Q and 2012 guidance, according to Leerink Swann. The problem is fixable but will require the device--which uses mild electrical pulses from an implanted device to stimulate the brain--to be off the market for 60-90 days, according to STJ's so-called "Dear Doctor" letter. "There have not been any serious patient injuries reported," Leerink says, but about 8 patients have needed to have the device removed and replaced because of inability to deliver the therapy. The device is not sold in the US. STJ shares were unchanged in after-hours trading. (george.stahl@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 5:44 (Dow Jones) A large part of the recent increase in foreign holdings of short-term Mexican Treasury notes known as Cetes stems from arbitrage opportunities, says Jaime Cortina, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Investors are buying Cetes to cover their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk, Cortina explains. MXN/USD at MXN12.8035 vs MXN12.7490 Wed close. (amy.guthrie@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 5:37 (Dow Jones) Exports of Mexican food products to China rose 75% in February with the same month last year, says Mexico's Agriculture Ministry. Last year, food exports to China totaled $142M. Agriculture officials have said Mexico is trying to diversify the markets for its food exports by participating in international food fairs and cultivating new business relationships. (jean.guerrero@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 5:33 (Dow Jones) As if Canadian shoppers needed any fresh incentives to cross the 49th parallel. The Canadian government in its fiscal 2012-13 budget raised the amount of money that Canadians can spend in the US before duties apply. The new rules allow Canadians to bring $200 worth of goods, duty-free, back into the country, for stays of more than 24 hours. That's up from $50. They can spend $800, up from $400, for stays of more than 48 hours. And they can spend $800 on goods for stays of more than a week, up from $750 now. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 5:30 (Dow Jones) Research In Motion (RIMM) CEO signals the company wouldn't be interested in any takeover bids. The "best way to drive value is to execute our plan to turn around" the company, Thorsten Heins says. That said, RIMM has launched strategic review to try to identify partnerships that leverage the company's BB10 phones, software and customer base to help in the turnaround effort, he says. RIMM also expects to announce new chief marketing officer "soon," Heins says. This has been a priority for Heins since his appointment as CEO in January. RIMM down 2.8% to $13.35 (ben.dummett@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-29-12 1824ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120329e83t000xg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
