\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Intervenes \highlight\uc2  More Despite Lower USD Inflow\b0\par\par\uc2 156 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 00:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 6:24 (Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts this week with no clear trigger for the actions, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  says. Late Monday the bank announced an auction to roll over the $2B reverse swap due April 2, again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market Wednesday with a dollar purchase estimated at $800M to $1.1B, possibly the biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market so far this year, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  says. Moreover, a fall-off in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows seems at odds with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive stance to curb the real's appreciation, with inflows sinking to $500M the week before last compared to a weekly $1.5B average, although still robust for the year to date, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  says. (diana.kinch@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-3100 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com [ 03-29-12 1824ET ]\par \par \uc2 1085 80000   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120329e83t000xf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
