\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Weaker On US Data,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 15:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Real opens at 1.8193/dollar versus BRL1.8107/dollar Tuesday\par \par \uc2 --Disappointing U.S. durable goods data hurt confidence\par \par \uc2 --Investors fret over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real weakened in early trading Wednesday on disappointing U.S. economic data and continued worries about possible market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Brazilian government.\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL1.8193 to the dollar early in the session, weaker against the Tuesday close of BRL1.8107, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., durable goods orders in February were up 2.2%, but that figure weighed in below market expectations of about 3.0%. The figures called into question the strength of the U.S. economic recovery at a time when investors are also worried about a possible recession in Europe and a slowdown in growth in China.\par \par \uc2 Worries about the pace of China's economic expansion hurt global commodities prices Wednesday, another factor counting against the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Lower commodities prices spell declining export revenues for Brazil.\par \par \uc2 "Meanwhile, Brazil's government is always keeping an eye on the market," said Wanderlei Muniz, a trader at southern \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Onnix brokerage. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible on any given day as the government keeps the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a box."\par \par \uc2 According to most traders and analysts, that "box" is currently between BRL1.80 to the dollar and BRL1.90.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian market becomes nervous whenever the real strengthens, especially when it gets close to the BRL1.80 mark.\par \par \uc2 "Brazilian exports are not competitive when the real is too strong," said former finance minister Antonio Delfim Netto. "Government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent a strengthening of the real is part of a legitimate defense of Brazilian interests."\par \par \uc2 In recent days, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come in the form of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of dollars from the market. In recent months, the government has also slapped higher taxes on certain forms of investment inflows. Higher taxes are especially worrisome for investors, because they create uncertainty and make long-term planning more difficult, according to analysts.\par \par \uc2 But Muniz said worries about Europe and China were also likely to be market factors for Brazil on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "It's obvious that the European troubles are not over yet," he said. Continued worries about Europe's debt crisis tend to reduce investment flows both to Europe and to emerging market countries.\par \par \uc2 -By Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3544-7090; brazil@dowjones.com [ 28-03-12 1307GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120328e83s000wl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
