\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's Real weakest in 11 weeks, Latam down\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 18:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso weakens 0.3 pct, Brazil real 0.56 pct\par \par \uc2 * Brazil cenbank holds auction to buy dollars\par \par \uc2 By Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, March 28 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened o n W ednesday after data showed lower-than-expected U.S. durable goods orders, while investors sold the Brazilian real in the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real slid to its weakest close since Jan. 9 to bid 1.8627 per dollar, with a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction to buy dollars contributing to its 0.56 percent depreciation.\par \par \uc2 Traders dumped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday on fears the government was preparing to expand the scope of a tax on financial transactions.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said on Wednesday the fears were not yet substantiated but were still a concern.\par \par \uc2 Even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already been weakening on Wednesday, the Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called an auction to buy U.S. dollars, setting the cutoff rate at 1.82 reais.\par \par \uc2 "They were trying to defend at 1.7 (reais per dollar) and they were successful in doing it, so now they have realized they can defend at 1.8 ... if they eventually move to 1.9 they will say: 'OK, let's defend at 1.9.' That's the approach of this government," said Diego Donadio, a \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  strategist in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers are trying to weaken a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  they say is too strong and hurts domestic manufacturers, made less competitive by cheap imports.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's government has raised its financial transactions, or "IOF," tax and extended its scope to foreign debt maturing in up to five years.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased dollars in the spot market in early February for the first time since September and the real has weakened around 6 percent since then.\par \par \uc2 The bank said on Wednesday it had purchased $1.896 billion so far this month.\par \par \uc2 "I'm very distressed about Brazil right now," said John Welch, emerging markets strategist and executive director at CIBC World Markets. "They are trying to get the dollar higher at a very high cost to the government and the country."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Mexico's peso weakened 0.3 percent to 12.509 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's only fully convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened as much as 0.77 percent after data showed new orders for U.S. manufactured goods slightly disappointed in February.\par \par \uc2 U.S. durable goods orders rose 2.2 percent last month, only partially reversing January's revised 3.6 percent decline in Mexico's top trade partner.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said riskier assets like emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were looking for an excuse to back off gains that followed comments from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's commitment to accommodative monetary policy on Monday and Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Economic growth in China and the debt crisis in Europe are still in the background, despite the United State's commitment to keeping borrowing costs low to spur growth.\par \par \uc2 "The market has had a bit of a run and investors don't trust it so they are trying to find anything to get out," said CIBC's Welch.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso ended 0.61 percent weaker, bidding 489 per dollar. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released a poll on Wednesday saying Chile's key interest rate will likely be on hold through October.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Caroline Stauffer; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120331e83s0007l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
