\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso slips on U.S. data, Brazil's real flat\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 17:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * U.S. data disappoints, hurts export-dependent Mexican peso\par \par \uc2 * Investors see Brazil cenbank defending real at 1.8\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso off 0.39 pct, Brazil real ends near flat\par \par \uc2 By Luciana Lopez and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK/RIO DE JANEIRO, March 21 (Reuters) - The Mexican and Chilean pesos weakened after disappointing U.S. housing data on Wednesday, while expectations of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbed enthusiasm for \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real.\par \par \uc2 U.S. home resales unexpectedly fell in February and the supply of properties on the market rose, causing investors to opt for low-risk assets like U.S. Treasuries rather than higher-yielding emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While U.S. employment figures have shown improvement and pointed to recovery in the world's largest economy, analysts point to persistent patches of weakness, such as the ongoing fallout from the 2008 subprime mortgage crisis.\par \par \uc2 "The data gives little indication that we have hit the bottom of this mortgage problem," said Enrique Alvarez, head of analysis at IDEAGlobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's economy is particularly tied to its northern neighbor, as it sends around 80 percent of its exports across the border. The Mexican peso dipped 0.39 percent to 12.7041 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso ended 0.19 percent weaker, bidding at 485.10 per dollar, its weakest close in a week.\par \par \uc2 Although Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Wednesday, discouraging U.S. data can in the longer term help emerging market assets by supporting bets that the U.S. Federal Reserve may yet move to inject a third round of liquidity into the market.\par \par \uc2 So-called quantitative easing has brought a flood of cash into Latin America's high-yielding assets in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also injected more than 1 trillion euros into the market through two three-year lending \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months.\par \par \uc2 "I expect a good portion of that money to end up in Latin America," said Alberto Bernal, head of fixed income research for Bulltick Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 "Those resources will continue to generate some important appreciation for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Bernal said.\par \par \uc2 REAL SEEN UNDERPERFORMING\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real ended just 0.09 percent weaker than its Tuesday close, bidding 1.819 per dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appeal has declined since the government started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market last month to contain its advance.\par \par \uc2 A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes the country's exports more expensive and therefore less competitive, spurring the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act. The real has lost more than 5 percent this month since authorities hardened their stance.\par \par \uc2 "The real is massively underperforming its peers," said strategist Diego Donadio of \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 He recommends selling Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of the Colombian or Mexican pesos as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer likely to tolerate a real stronger than 1.8 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it had purchased $1.214 billion on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market between March 1 and March 16.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120324e83l0007z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
