\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Volatile On China Growth, Government  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 14:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real falls with more concerns about China\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Treasury could be more active on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian traders expect the real to remain volatile Tuesday\par \par \uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes and Matthew Cowley\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened sharply Tuesday morning, amid considerable volatility, as traders played catch up with more concerns about China economic growth, and fretted about Brazilian government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Negative comments on China from \uc2 BHP Billiton\uc2  and \uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2  once again raised concerns about the pace of slowdown there, which could have an impact on demand for Brazil's raw materials, including iron ore.\par \par \uc2 "The day will remain volatile, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  vulnerable to the international news, specially coming from Asia", said Mauro Araujo, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at Sao Paulo's brokerage Vision Corretora.\par \par \uc2 Alfredo Barbutti, economist at brokerage BGC Liquidez Corretora agreed. "Today, the real is being affected by the trend in the Australian dollar," he added.\par \par \uc2 China's iron-ore demand is "flattening," according to Ian Ashby, BHP's head of iron ore, while David Joyce, \uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2 's managing director of iron-ore output, said China's economy was "slowing." Their comments came at a news conference at the Australian Journal of Mining global iron-ore conference in Perth.\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL1.8292, weaker than the BRL1.8055 late Monday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, investors were also digesting a newspaper report in Brazil, which suggested the Brazilian National Treasury will take a more active role in the government's efforts to contain the appreciation of the Brazilian real versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury may buy back up to $15 billion in overseas debts ahead of schedule to ease pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a report in Tuesday's edition of the O Estado de S. Paulo newspaper.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Estado, Treasury Secretary Arno Augustin said the government is already in talks to pay back ahead of schedule a $2.9 billion loan from the Inter-American Development Bank, or IDB.\par \par \uc2 Estado said the comments indicated that the government isn't satisfied with the current level of BRL1.80 per dollar, and that it wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken further.\par \par \uc2 Augustin said that the Treasury's efforts are part of a broad government strategy in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and that the government will continue to "surprise" market players with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures.\par \par \uc2 Treasury officials weren't immediately available for comment Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the official said the Treasury may buy back foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt to help prevent Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating too sharply.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real appreciated by about 10% against the dollar earlier this year before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government took a series of measures that have so far managed to push the real back to 1.80 to the dollar in the most recent session.\par \par \uc2 -By Luciana Magalhaes and Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 11 3544 7082; brazil@dowjones.com [ 20-03-12 1311GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120320e83k000s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
