\par\par \b \uc2 JP Morgan \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  CEO Sees Real Weaker On Rate Cuts,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 892 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 20:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\uc2 J.P. Morgan\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief executive sees \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker on lower rates, government measures\par \par \uc2 --Berquo: Over medium term, pressures on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate will remain\par \par \uc2 --Berquo: Brazil capital-market activity is better than expected in early 2012\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Rogerio Jelmayer and Matthew Cowley \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real will weaken in the short term, given falling interest rates and government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Claudio Berquo, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief executive of \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (\f28 \uc2 \f2 JPM\f28 \uc2 \f2 ).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is much more vigilant and it's clear that when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gets close to BRL1.70 the red lights come on," Berquo said during an interview at his office in Sao Paulo. He sees the real staying in a range of around BRL1.80 to BRL1.90 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last week, Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its key rate, the Selic, to 9.75%, and Wednesday it indicated it will continue to cut rates, although it said they won't get as far as the historical low of 8.75%. The government also has unleashed a series of measures, from buying dollars to imposing taxes on some capital flows, to arrest the real's momentum.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Having touched BRL1.69 at the end of February, the Brazilian real has given back some of its gains; Friday, it traded at BRL1.80 per dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As interest rates come down, Brazil's local banks will have to adjust, moving away from their reliance on government bonds and developing new products, Berquo said, adding \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  sees this as an opportunity to offer its products.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government, meanwhile, also must tread carefully, as Brazil will have to adjust to lower levels of interest rates, Berquo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are very enthusiastic about this but at the same time you have to be careful otherwise there could be a surprise," Berquo said. "You never know if there are going to be collateral effects."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Those investors who traditionally have parked their cash in high-yielding government bonds will start looking for other options, such as shares. But Berquo said even if a small part of that was to be diverted to equities, "there's not enough paper."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is the ever-present threat of inflation, which is "the main enemy of all of us," Berquo said, adding the government could help with that by containing spending.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, is likely to remain under pressure to appreciate over the medium- to long-term. Even if short-term investors withdraw, there will be more long-term foreign-direct investment, Berquo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two years ago, \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  added a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  team to handle flow transactions--low-margin, high-volume \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  contracts that are a booming business and allow \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  to get a feeling for what is going on in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian government's steps to contain the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have had relatively little impact on companies or long-term investors, Berquo said. Most established Brazilian corporations that borrow overseas now take out 10-year loans; if companies aren't in that category, they have the option of a private placement, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The steps may help develop the local corporate-bond market, which is practically nonexistent today. With interest rates coming down and companies locked out of the medium-term overseas market, local-bond sales "could start to fly," Berquo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's capital market has had a better start in 2012 than had been expected back in September and October, when the view appeared to be bleak, he said. "This year is the year of debt," Berquo said, adding he also expects to see a number of important share offerings. Much of the work will have to be done in the first part of the year, as the market will dry up as the U.S. election cycle gets under way later in the year, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Overseas bonds issued by Brazilian companies soared in the first two months of 2012, as global markets leapt back to life after six months of worrying about European debts, according to the Brazilian Association of Capital Market Institutions, or Anbima.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nonetheless, \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  is slowing down its pace of growth in Brazil this year, preferring to absorb its recent rapid expansion and see how the market develops this year. After the bank tripled its staff in three years, it has 900 employees in Brazil, and plans to add around 50 more this year, Berquo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil is "overbanked," with every major global player already present in a market of well-capitalized and extremely competitive local players, the executive said. \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  is careful not to go up against local banking giants such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Itau Unibanco Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  SA (ITUB, ITUB4.BR) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Bradesco SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BBD, BBDC4.BR, BBDO) in the areas in which they are strongest, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We want to be more local than the foreigners and more foreign than the locals," Berquo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  doesn't have immediate plans for acquisitions in Brazil, Berquo said, either because there aren't players or they are too expensive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Rogerio Jelmayer and Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 11 3544 7082; rogerio.jelmayer@dowjones.com [ 16-03-12 1937GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1833   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120316e83g00129\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
