\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Ends Up-And-Down Session Nearly Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 506 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 21:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real, after being pushed and pulled between international optimism and domestic concerns, settled Thursday virtually unchanged from the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL1.7693 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with Wednesday's close of BRL1.7680.\par \par \uc2 Traders said volume was relatively light, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuated in a fairly wide range. After opening stronger at BRL1.7595, the real weakened around midday to BRL1.78 before recovering in later trading.\par \par \uc2 The volatility came as the market eyed a variety of relevant headlines.\par \par \uc2 Hopes for a solid participation rate by private creditors in Greece's bond swap buoyed overseas markets from Shanghai to Wall Street.\par \par \uc2 But in Brazil, investors are concerned that local authorities have become less tolerant of a strong real than they were last year, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied to BRL1.54 before a deterioation in Europe's debt crisis sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a tailspin.\par \par \uc2 Though the Finance Ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unleashed a variety of measures last year to curb the real's appreciation, including taxes and near-daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy was coming off one of its best years in decades, having grown 7.5% in 2010.\par \par \uc2 By comparison, gross domestic product expanded by a paltry 2.7% in 2011, with the industrial sector's particularly sluggish growth attributed by Brazilian authorities to a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that hurt exports and encouraged imports. Data released this week then showed a sharp downturn in January's industrial production, suggesting this year could also be difficult for factories.\par \par \uc2 "There's all kinds of news that the government is preparing more measures," said Joao Medeiros, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at Sao Paulo's Pioneer brokerage. "[Finance Minister Guido] Mantega supposedly can't sleep at night because of all the capital that's entering the country."\par \par \uc2 Brazil received heavy financial flows at the start of the year as local companies took advantage of happy times in global markets to cheaply place debt abroad. By late February, the real pushed below the BRL1.70 level for the first time in four months, after closing 2011 at BRL1.8642.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 0.75 percentage point reduction of the benchmark Selic interest rate Wednesday could make the real less appealing to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators attracted by the large differential with rates in other countries.\par \par \uc2 But even if the bank hacks Selic all the way to 8.5%--as a growing number of economists project after Wednesday's bigger-than-expected cut--Brazil will still have among the highest interest rates in the world.\par \par \uc2 "Brazil remains attractive for foreign investors, even with this cut," said Joao Querino de Santos, a trader at Sao Paulo's J. Alves brokerage.\par \par \uc2 -By Paul Kiernan, Dow Jones Newswires; (+55)11-3544-7074, paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 08-03-12 2010GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120308e83800152\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
