\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Brazil industry slumps again, eyes on c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 13:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Industrial production falls more than expected\par \par \uc2 * Weak manufacturing weighing heavily on economic growth\par \par \uc2 * Numbers bolster argument for bigger interest rate cut\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Asher Levine\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, March 7 (Reuters) - A slump in Brazil's industrial production in January was nearly three times worse than analysts had expected, putting pressure on policymakers to take action as manufacturers struggle against the tide of a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a heavy tax load.\par \par \uc2 The data may bolster expectations of a sharper \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate cut later on Wednesday, a day after disappointing data showed Latin America's largest economy expanded just 2.7 percent in 2011, prompting pledges of aggressive stimulus measures from the government.\par \par \uc2 Interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> fell across the board following the data release.\par \par \uc2 Industrial production in Brazil fell 2.1 percent in January from December, government statistics agency IBGE said on Wednesday. It was the worst performance since a similar fall in April 2011.\par \par \uc2 Production had been expected to fall 0.8 percent, according to the median estimate of 20 analysts in a Reuters survey. The forecasts ranged from a 1.3 percent drop to a 0.3 percent decline.\par \par \uc2 January's industrial production contracted 3.4 percent from a year earlier, more than double the 1.5 percent drop forecast in the Reuters survey. Estimates for output ranged from a 2.1 percent drop to a 0.3 percent decline.\par \par \uc2 "The industrial sector has been a drag on overall real GDP," \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  analyst Alberto Ramos wrote in a note to investors on Wednesday. Ramos expects the performance of the industrial sector to improve slightly throughout 2012 but to continue to lag overall real GDP growth.\par \par \uc2 Manufacturers have blamed most of their problems on Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, which has strengthened about 40 percent since the depths of the financial crisis in 2009 and 6 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 In response, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent weeks, while Finance Minister Guido Mantega on Tuesday promised to support Brazil's flagging industrial sector with tax incentives and other unspecified stimulus measures.\par \par \uc2 "All the research shows exactly what we've been saying for quite some time about the deindustrialization process the country is experiencing," said Paulo Skaf, president of Sao Paulo state industry federation Fiesp, one of the country's most powerful industrial lobbies. "Now all that's missing is for the government to take the correct measures to face it."\par \par \uc2 Of the 27 industrial sectors surveyed, 14 shrank in January from December, including cars, mining and medical equipment.\par \par \uc2 In broader industrial categories, output of capital goods fell 16 percent for the month, the IBGE said. Production of consumer goods fell 0.1 percent month on month, and durable consumer goods dropped 1.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 Fourth-quarter earnings were a miss for most listed manufacturing companies in Brazil, signaling the shrinking role of industry as services take center stage. Many of those companies, especially miners, pulp and food processors and capital goods makers, are revising down their future investment plans to cope with a tougher economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 For details on the IBGE industrial output figures see: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://ibge.gov.br/home/presidencia/noticias/noticia_visualiza.php?id_noticia=2094"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://ibge.gov.br/home/presidencia/noticias/noticia_visualiza.php?id_noticia=2094}}}\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Asher Levine; Editing by Jeffrey Benkoe and James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/INDUSTRY (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | ABX | BNX | FUN | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120307e837000oq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
