\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real slips on cenbank action, Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 2012\par 17:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  beats back real's surge\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real weakens 1.2 pct, Chile peso declines 0.6 pct\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso trades flat\par \par \uc2 By Rachel Uranga and Asher Levine\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, Feb 29 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real slipped sharply on Wednesday after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to beat back the real's surge beyond the 1.70-per-dollar mark.\par \par \uc2 The real, which has appreciated more than eight percent since the beginning of the year, weakened 1.2 percent to bid at 1.7190 per dollar. Other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded mixed.\par \par \uc2 "With foreign capital entering the local market, it will continue to get more difficult to hold the real at this level," said Maurico Nakahodo, an economist at Brazil's CM Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 A flood of foreign investors seeking returns higher than those found in developed countries has helped strengthen the real, hurting local manufactures by increasing the cost of the country's exports.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday that U.S. dollar inflows to the country totaled $5.251 billion in the calendar month through February 24.\par \par \uc2 "Both the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as expectations that the government could employ other tools to hold back the real's gains helped weaken the real," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and spot dollar buys to cool the real.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 30,500, or 76 percent, of the 40,000 reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps on offer in the auction for a financial value of about $1.5 billion. The contracts mimic the purchase of dollars in futures markets.\par \par \uc2 In Peru, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts have failed to slow gains for the sol. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its strongest level in 15 years, advancing 0.11 percent to 2.673 per dollar despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purchase of $118 million in the spot market, its third consecutive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso traded flat at 12.8321 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trimmed early gains after banks gobbled up more than half a trillion euros of cheap three-year funds offered by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to stabilize the euro-zone financial system.\par \par \uc2 Stronger-than-expected U.S. fourth-quarter growth data bolstered an early firming of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But comments by Federal Reserve chairman Ben Bernanke, warning that the U.S. job market is far from normal, limited advances.\par \par \uc2 Bernanke told the U.S. Congress that unless growth accelerated, the unacceptably high U.S. unemployment rate would not keep dropping. But he stopped short of signaling further Fed bond purchases, tempering traders' hopes for monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2 "Some see Bernanke's comments as an indication there will be no monetary stimulus in the short term," said Sergio Tricio, head of studies with \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile, a brokerage in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso weakened 0.65 percent to bid at 479.80 per dollar. Declining copper prices - Chile's main export - also contributed to the weakening of the peso.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Peter Murphy in Brasilia, Moises Avila in Santiago and Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City; Editing by Padraic Cassidy)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | E | RBN | M | D | NAT | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120303e82t0008w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
