\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real slips beyond 1.70 after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 2012\par 14:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ratchets up attack on stronger real\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells 76 percent of reverse swaps at auction\par \par \uc2 * Real bucks regional \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  firming after ECB cash injection\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds background)\par \par \uc2 By Silvio Cascione\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 29 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and bought dollars in the spot market on Wednesday, keeping Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating beyond the 1.70 per dollar mark.\par \par \uc2 The real, which had firmed to 1.6860 in early trading, its strongest in four months, weakened after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 1.7138.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real to avoid the surge seen in other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (ECB) offer of 530 billion euros of cheap finance to Europe's troubled banks.\par \par \uc2 The real has gained more than 9 percent since the beginning of the year on the back of massive inflows from investors seeking higher returns than they can get in more developed markets. Brazil's benchmark interest rate is 10.5 percent. In the United States the equivalent rate is zero to 0.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 The ECB's capital injection pumped even more low cost capital into world markets. Much of it is expected to move to higher-risk and higher-return assets in places such as Latin America.\par \par \uc2 A stronger Brazilian real has made the country's exports more expensive and hurt the competitiveness of local manufactuers prompting the Brazilian government to act.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 30,500, or 76 percent, of the 40,000 reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps on offer in the auction for a financial value of about $1.5 billion. The contracts mimic the purchase of dollars in futures markets.\par \par \uc2 The bank sold 20,000, 32-day reverse swaps maturing April 2,\par \par \uc2 99.9661 percent of face value for a nominal yield of 0.3941 percent and financial value of $999.7 million.\par \par \uc2 It also sold 10,500, 123-day reverse swaps maturing July 2, at 99.6850 percent of face value for a nominal yield of 0.9408 percent and financial value of $523.3 million.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Brazil's real underperformed the Mexican and the Colombian pesos , which rose 0.5 and 0.15 percent to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold only 3,500 contracts in a similar \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It also bought U.S. dollar forwards and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local spot market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Alexandre Tombini said on Tuesday that those auctions helped prevent the real from strengthening too much. National Treasury Secretary Arno Augustin also said that the country's sovereign wealth fund could buy dollars.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's speeding economic growth has been attracting foreign investments in infrastructure, bonds and equities. Its 10.5-percent benchmark interest rates also lures investors.,\par \par \uc2 The govenrnment is pursuing a tighter fiscal policy to pave the way for single-digit rates.\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's push to shield its financial system by lending more than 1 trillion euros to banks made cheap money even more available in global markets.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Silvio Cascione; Editing by Jeb Blount)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /SWAP (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120229e82t000vr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
