\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil says  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  strategy focuses on c.bank action\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2012\par 21:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Feb 28 (Reuters) - Brazil's government could use its sovereign wealth fund to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, but for now will focus on a strategy of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases, National Treasury Secretary Arno Augustin said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The statement hints at a lower probability of direct dollar purchases from the Brazilian sovereign fund anytime soon. It came even as Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, strengthened past the 1.70 per U.S. dollar mark on Tuesday for the first time in four months, despite recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The sovereign fund can be used to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market not only with its available resources, but also by using bonds" in its portfolio, Augustin said. "There is such a possibility, but we haven't adopted that as of yet. We maintain our policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases."\par \par \uc2 The real has gained about 10 percent this year against the dollar as low interest rates abroad have driven global investors seeking higher returns to pour money into Brazil. The Brazilian government has sought to limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise because of the negative effects on exports and competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian s Finance Minister Guido Mantega, who coined the expression "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war," has vowed to used \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sovereign wealth fund "at any time" to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 In August, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sovereign fund had 15 billion reais ($9 bln) in assets, according to data released by the country's securities and exchange regulator.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 1.7 reais)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tiago Pariz, Writing by Silvio Cascione; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /TREASURY  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120228e82s001al\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
