\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real firms despite cenbank, rates eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2012\par 16:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with closing prices, Colombia raising rates)\par \par \uc2 * Real gains despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions to buy dlrs\par \par \uc2 * Colombia extends dollar purchases through August, peso flat\par \par \uc2 * Brazil neutral interest rates seen higher than expected\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso weakens on euro zone concerns\par \par \uc2 By Jos\u233\'00\'E9 de Castro\par \par \uc2 Feb 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real gained on Friday as persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to fully absorb dollar inflows, while the country's interest-rate futures rose sharply after a survey suggested the economy needed tighter monetary policy to grow without higher inflation.\par \par \uc2 Most Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were supported by commodity gains, although worries about the euro zone crisis weighed on the Mexican peso. Colombia's decision to extend dollar purchases through August could also curb a rally in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real trimmed some of its earlier gains, but still closed 0.23 percent higher at 1.710 per dollar after two dollar-buying auctions launched by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  less than one hour apart.\par \par \uc2 The bank's action came one day after it offered to sell reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps for the first time since August and also bought dollars in the spot market, in an attempt to halt a rally that has been hurting the country's exporters.\par \par \uc2 The real has gained more than 9 percent so far this year and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market added to the perception that the government is drawing a line at 1.7 reais per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The psychological level has inevitably shaped around the 1.7000-handle in spot, though clearly the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is struggling to absorb the large debt inflows related primarily to external corporate debt issuance and overall strong capital account inflows," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBS Securities.\par \par \uc2 At Friday's auctions, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially bought dollars at a cutoff price 1.7059 reais, and then at 1.7057 reais.\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES JUMP\par \par \uc2 Concerns about the pace of monetary policy easing in Brazil were stoked after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released a survey showing economists estimate the economy can grow without inflationary pressures if real interest rates are about 5.5 percent, higher than the 4.5-5.0 percent expected by many traders.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's benchmark interest rate currently stands at 10.5 percent after four half-percentage-point rate cuts since August. Inflation for the 12 months ended Jan. 31 was 6.22 percent, giving Brazil a real interest rate of about 4.3 percent - more than a percentage point below the neutral rate survey estimate.\par \par \uc2 "There is this feeling that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be exaggerating and, just to be sure, markets raised the rates," said a trader in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's interest-rate contract for January 2013 rose to 9.270 percent from 9.220 percent in Thursday's adjusted close. The contract for January 2014 jumped to 9.750 percent from 9.670 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso rose as much as 0.7 percent during the session before ending broadly flat against the dollar, at 480.30, as local dollar purchases offset a jump in prices of copper, the country's main export.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, however, concerns about the euro zone crisis drove the peso 0.65 percent lower to a one-week low of 12.9055 per dollar, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's closing prices.\par \par \uc2 After trading within a narrow range in the past few days, the peso pierced a key Fibonacci resistance level around 12.86 per greenback, but analysts said light trading made it unclear whether those losses will be sustained.\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA TO BUY MORE DOLLARS\par \par \uc2 Strong dollar inflows have provided a powerful tailwind to Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, and analysts expect that trend to intensify as commodity prices rise and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  floods the markets again with cheap money next week.\par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso gained as much as 0.4 percent during the day, but closed little changed at 1,776.00 per dollar, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its widely-expected decision to raise benchmark interest rates by 25 basis points to 5.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 The bank also said it will extend its dollar-buying program, which includes daily purchases of a minimum of $20 million in the spot market, for at least three additional months until Aug. 4.\par \par \uc2 "We would expect this to help prevent further appreciation of the peso, but do not expect a reversion of the trend from recent months," \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Nelson Bocanegra in Bogota, writing by Walter Brandimarte; editing by Theodore d'Afflisio, Gary Crosse)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2) | ABN | 