\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Stocks Close Lower On Pessimistic Outlook For Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2012\par 21:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --The Ibovespa index fell 0.4% to 65,819, from Wednesday's close of 66,092 points\par \par \uc2 --Pessimistic growth forecasts from Europe outweighed good news from U.S., Brazil\par \par \uc2 --European Commission forecast euro-zone GDP will contract in 2012\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazilian stocks closed lower Thursday after bad news from Europe outweighed positive indicators in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Ibovespa index fell 0.4% to 65,819 points, from Wednesday's close of 66,092 points.\par \par \uc2 The euro-zone economy is expected to contract in 2012, after falling into a recession at the start of the year, the European Commission warned Thursday. On an annual basis, the 17-country euro zone is forecast to contract by 0.3%, while gross domestic product in the larger European Union is seen flat on the year. The commission said it expects the euro-zone economy to contract in the first quarter by 0.3%, after dropping by the same amount in the last quarter of 2011.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Mario Draghi added to the pessimism about growth, by insisting that the region's worsening economic situation not be used as an excuse to relax deficit targets.\par \par \uc2 "There is no feasible trade-off" between economic overhauls and fiscal belt-tightening, Draghi said in an interview with The Wall Street Journal, his first since Greece sealed its second bailout deal.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's Labor Ministry announced shortly after the market opened that 118,895 jobs with formal documentation were created in January, even though this was 21.83% below the figure for the same month in 2011. The mining, services, construction and agricultural industries were the biggest job creators in the month, while the number of new jobs in the government administrative sector fell, as well as in the retail sector for seasonal reasons, the Ministry said.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., the number of new claims for unemployment benefits remained stable in the week ending Feb. 18, a more favorable result than had been expected by analysts.\par \par \uc2 The good jobs news from the U.S. wasn't enough to buoy markets in Brazil, said Pedro Paulo Silveira, an economist at the TOV brokerage house in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "The market started falling because of the outlook in Europe," he said. "The U.S. data today don't change the pessimistic trend that the European information started."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday, holding a reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction at which $174.7 million in contracts were sold. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also failed to cheer equities investors.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthened to BRL1.6978 to the U.S. dollar, from its Wednesday close of BRL1.7051.\par \par \uc2 Blue-chips showed mixed performance.\par \par \uc2 Oil producer \uc2 Petroleo Brasileiro\uc2  (PBR, PETR4.BR) gained 0.1% to BRL23.92 ($13.99), on rising oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Mining company Vale (VALE, VALE5.BR) gained 2% to BRL42.80.\par \par \uc2 Steelmaker \uc2 Usinas Siderurgicas de Minas Gerais\uc2  (USIM5.BR) slipped 1% to BRL11.87.\par \par \uc2 Utility \uc2 Companhia Energetica de Sao Paulo\uc2  (CESP6.BR) fell 2.6% to BRL36.93.\par \par \uc2 -By Jeffrey T. Lewis, Dow Jones Newswires; jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com [ 23-02-12 2048GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1836 5053 5076   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120223e82n001b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
