\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Weaker After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2 ;More Action Seen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Diana Kinch   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2012\par 21:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real weakened in late trading Thursday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice to stem a trend that has led the real to appreciate 9% against the U.S. dollar so far this year. Economists expect further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming days.\par \par \uc2 The real exited normal trading at BRL1.7094 to the U.S. dollar, weaker than Wednesday's close of BRL1.7051, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day however, the real had strengthened to BRL 1.6978, tracking the euro and markets world-wide in a positive response to a measure of German business confidence that rose more than expected. Germany's IFO business climate index rose to 109.60 in February, from 108.30 in January, and above market expectations of 108.80.\par \par \uc2 The early strengthening of the real put the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above the BRL1.70 barrier that economists view as an unofficial trigger point above which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to take action to prevent excessive appreciation, which puts Brazilian exporters at a disadvantage on international markets.\par \par \uc2 Shortly afterward, the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a sale of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and a spot auction to purchase dollars, managing to push the real back to BRL1.7093, the other side of the barrier.\par \par \uc2 "They won't admit it, but BRL1.70 may be a barrier for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jankiel Santos of Espirito Santo Investment Bank. "Their actions stemmed the appreciation and had the desired effect."\par \par \uc2 For Raphael Martello of Tendencias Consultancy, the government showed itself to be "a bit bothered" by the real's crossing the BRL1.70 mark. "The real is one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that's appreciated the most so far this year," the economist said.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold only a fraction of the reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts it offered at the first auction, this nonetheless helped stabilize the market, setting the level back at around BRL1.70, which was consolidated by the later dollar purchase auction, according to Martello.\par \par \uc2 Both economists said they expect further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming days, as foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows continue strongly as Brazil is considered an attractive investment destination due to its continuing high interest rates and strong economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The measures are likely to include more dollar purchase auctions and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions, but are less likely to include new taxes on foreign investment, they said.\par \par \uc2 "Brazil needs foreign investments to finance its growth as local savings levels are low," Martello said.\par \par \uc2 -By Diana Kinch, Dow Jones Newswires. Tel 55 21 2586 6086 diana.kinch@dowjones.com [ 23-02-12 2008GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120223e82n001av\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
