\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Strengthens To BRL1.69 In Early Trading;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Foreseen\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2012\par 13:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthened past the BRL1.70 to the U.S. dollar threshold in early trading Thursday, tracking gains in the euro, after a measure of German business confidence rose more than expected.\par \par \uc2 The real traded at BRL1.6978 to the dollar at 1142 GMT, stronger than its Wednesday exit from active trading at BRL1.7051, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 After a stable pre-market, the real strengthened after the announcement that Germany's IFO business climate index rose to 109.60 in February, from 108.30 in January, and above market expectations of 108.80.\par \par \uc2 The real strengthened despite continuing uncertainties over the future of the euro zone, giving rise to traders' speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to buy dollars at auction in a move to curb appreciation of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at an auction for BRL1.7083 to the dollar but still didn't manage to stop the real strengthening during the day, as expectations continue of strong foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows ahead, as Brazil continues to be seen as a desirable investment destination.\par \par \uc2 The euro-zone backdrop continued gloomy after the European Commission said that the zone's economy could contract 0.3% in 2012, from a previous forecast of 0.5% growth.\par \par \uc2 Traders said that Europe could be preparing itself for Greece's eventual exit from the euro-zone due to the continuing contamination of the regional economy from Greece's debt problems. Uncertainties over the country's debt restructuring process continue in the run up to the vote later Thursday by the Greek parliament on the law project allowing the government to proceed with the private sector debt restructuring.\par \par \uc2 -By Diana Kinch, Dow Jones Nedwswires. Tel 55 21 2586 6086 diana.kinch@dowjones.com [ 23-02-12 1235GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120223e82n000yh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
