\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Weaker On Lingering Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan and Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2012\par 21:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt were weaker mostly as investor confidence ebbed on worries that Greece's bailout may not be enough in the long run.\par \par \uc2 However, some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were stronger against the dollar due to local policy action. For instance, South Africa said it plans to embark on its infrastructure action plan as a way to create jobs and tame the country's ballooning 24% unemployment rate. In Latin America, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Peru helped weaken their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' gain on the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Risk premiums on emerging market debt was just a tad firmer at 366 basis points over comparable Treasury yields on the \uc2 J. P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Market Bond Index Global. Risk premiums on Chile and Russia's debt was weaker. Venezuela, once again, was a stronger performer as investors were bullish on the possibility of change in its central administration during the October elections. Risk premiums on its five-year credit default swaps tightened by 15 basis points Wednesday, according to Markit data., while risk premiums on its sovereign debt firmed up 38 basis points to 980 basis points over comparable Treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 The City of Buenos Aires was back in the market with a $415 million five-year bond at 9.95%, according to a person familiar with the deal. The deal hasn't priced yet.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the capital city of Argentina backed away from selling this bond as Greece's problems weighed on investor confidence.\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  front, the South African rand managed to stay stronger to the dollar all day long despite the broader market weakness. This is unusual for the rand to buck the broader trend, since it usually is a proxy for risk meaning it is weaker against the dollar when investor confidence is on the wane and stronger when confidence is on the rise. The dollar was at ZAR7.7294, after hitting a low of ZAR7.7018, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that bucked the trend Wednesday were supported by their central banks. For instance, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the spot market to buy dollars at BRL1.7083 to the dollar. Similarly, Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at PEN2.680 against the dollar. The dollar was trading at BRL1.7064 against the real, weaker by 0.5% from its Tuesday's close at BRL1.7146, according to CQG data, while the dollar was unchanged to the Peruvian peso at PEN2.680--the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases.\par \par \uc2 -By Prabha Natarajan, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2468; prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com @djfxtrader [ 22-02-12 2057GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120222e82m0018g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
