\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latin America  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains on Greece bailout hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2012\par 16:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Real spot market closed Mon and Tues for Carnaval holiday\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso gains 0.4 pct, Brazil's real firms 0.11 pct\par \par \uc2 By Jean Luis Arce and Alonso Soto\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/BRASILIA, Feb 17 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Friday as investors cautiously bet a Greek bailout deal would be struck on Monday, helping the country avert a messy default.\par \par \uc2 Against the U.S. dollar, Brazil's real appreciated 0.11 percent to 1.7140 while Mexico's peso gained 0.44 to bid at 12.7560.\par \par \uc2 Euro zone finance ministers are expected to finalize the details of a Greek rescue package on Monday but Eurogroup head Jean-Claude Juncker said there was still much work to be done to draw down the country's soaring debt.\par \par \uc2 After months of diplomatic hurdles and alternating market optimism and fear over whether Greece would avoid a chaotic default, investors remain wary ahead of the meeting.\par \par \uc2 "There is a moderate optimism that they are going to approve a second bailout package for Greece," said Erick Urtuzuastegui, an analyst at consultancy Prognosis in Mexico City. "There is every indication that in the short term there won't be a disorderly Greek default and that lowers risk aversion."\par \par \uc2 The real and the Mexican peso both gained about 0.4 percent this week. The Mexican peso traded between 12.6688 and 12.9943 per dollar this week while the real ran between 1.7090 and 1.7375.\par \par \uc2 "We are in a very narrow range and I don't think that is going to change until after a decision is made in Greece," said Enrique Alvarez, Latin America bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with IDEAGlobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have soared this year, largely on hopes the euro zone debt crisis could be easing and on signs of a recovering economy in the United States.\par \par \uc2 "The confirmation of that deal next week will probably get investors to seek higher-yield assets," said Reginaldo Galhardo, exchange trade manager for Treviso Corretora in Sao Paulo. "All that liquidity in more conservative positions will return to emerging markets with force."\par \par \uc2 Galhardo said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are likely to push the real closer to the 1.70 per dollar mark to test the tolerance level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government.\par \par \uc2 In February, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the real gained more than 8 percent on a surge in risk appetite that has boosted other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The market is testing the resolve of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government," Galhardo said.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real spot market will be closed on Monday and Tuesday due to the Carnaval holiday.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso ended flat, firming 0.06 to bid at 484.50 per dollar after prices for its main export fell.\par \par \uc2 (additional reporting by Rachel Uranga; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120220e82h000tr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
