\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  firms, Venezuelan bonds jump after primary\b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2012\par 19:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real hits 3-1/2 mo high, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  eyed\par \par \uc2 * Venezuela bonds gain on opposition leaders strong showing\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains 0.71 pct, Mexico's strengthens 0.76 pct\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Rachel Uranga and Daniel Bases\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/NEW YORK, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Brazil's real firmed to a 3-1/2 month high on Monday, raising concerns of interevention, while Venezuelan bonds gained after the opposition rallied behind a candidate to battle socialist president Hugo Chavez.\par \par \uc2 Greece's parliament approved tough austerity measures needed for a new bailout, which lifted appetite for riskier assets around the world and helped Brazil's real and Mexico's peso\par \par \uc2 bounce back from their sharpest weekly losses in two months\par \par \uc2 last week.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso strengthened 0.76 percent to 12.6955\par \par \uc2 per dollar , recovering much of its slump last week,\par \par \uc2 while Brazil's real bid 0.71 percent stronger at 1.7145 per dollar, its strongest close since the end of October.\par \par \uc2 "Most of the so-called risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are doing better in the wake of the Greek austerity package being passed," said Clyde Wardle, emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Despite Monday's parliamentary approval, the Greek government remained under pressure to convince a skeptical euro zone that it would abide by the terms of a multi-billion-euro rescue package. European finance ministers meet on Wednesday to discuss the bailout package.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said gains in riskier assets may be limited after a huge rally at the start of the year. Further milstones need to be met in the coming weeks to ease concerns of a chaotic default by Greece. "I don't think there's huge enthusiasm that we are out of the woods by any stretch," Wardle said.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about Greece last week ate into a surge in Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year made on the back of\par \par \uc2 improved economic data in China and the United States, along with hopes the euro zone's debt crisis would ease.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also looking forward to another round of cheap bank funding from the ECB later this month, while some are betting on another round of asset purchases by the U.S. Federal Reserve could further support demand for higher yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 Last month the Fed said it envisions exceptionally low interest rates through late 2014. Low interest rates in major economies drive investors to seek higher yields in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The sharp gains are pressuring the margins of Latin American exporters, since stronger local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  make the region's manufacturers less competitive against cheaper imports while also making their exports more expensive.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its spot market for the first time last week since September, and traders said they were expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take further measures to curb the recent appreciation of the real.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela's bonds outperformed their emerging market peers after opposition presidential candidate Henrique Capriles'\par \par \uc2 strong showing in his party's primary stirred hopes that the center-left former governor could unseat Chavez.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela's benchmark 2027 Global bond bid up a point in price to 80.75, pushing its yield down 17 basis points to 12.124 percent, its lowest since late April 2010.\par \par \uc2 Sovereign U.S. dollar denominated bond yields spread over comparable U.S. Treasuries narrowed roughly 32 basis points compared to 9 basis points of tightening for the overall benchmark \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela, by far the country with the largest yield spread on the EMBI+, is trading 996 basis points over U.S. Treasuries versus 335 basis points for the index itself.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso bid 0.25 percent weaker at 479.90\par \par \uc2 per dollar, pulling back from a five-month high last week as the price for copper, the country's top export, slipped.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Michael O'Boyle;Editing by Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120216e82d0018l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
