\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Weaker On Lack Of Accord In Greece: More Volatility Seen\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2012\par 13:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones) -- Brazil's real weakened in early trading Thursday, tracking the euro, after Greece's political parties failed to reach an accord on austerity measures seen as essential for the country to qualify for a bailout package to ease its debt problems.\par \par \uc2 The real traded at BRL1.7236 to the dollar at 1218 GMT, compared with BRL1.7178 Wednesday, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Traders said further volatility could occur in the run up to a euro-zone meeting of ministers later Thursday to discuss the possibility of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  getting involved in Greece's debt restructuring. This follows a protracted meeting between the Greek government and political party leaders, who wouldn't accept a cut of EUR300 million in benefits cuts, including retirement pensions. According to local sources, Sunday will be the deadline for the cuts to be agreed, allowing Greece to proceed with talks on a debt restructuring accord with creditors.\par \par \uc2 Market players also expressed concern that rising inflation in China could make expected cuts in interest rates less likely in the near future. Chinese consumer inflation rose 4.5% in January from a year earlier, from 4.1% in December.\par \par \uc2 Nervousness continues in the market in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid talk that new \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may occur to avoid appreciation of the real after several days of heavy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows, partly from a succession of company bond issues overseas.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the third time in four sessions, purchasing dollars via forward-delivery contracts.\par \par \uc2 -By Diana Kinch, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 , Tel +55 21 2586 6086. diana.kinch@dowjones.com [ 09-02-12 1232GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120209e8290015z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
