\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Traders Expecting More  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2012\par 12:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 6:46 (Dow Jones) Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers are expecting further government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, according to a dealer at a major bank. The timing depends on events in Greece. "If there is good news from Greece today about a debt agreement, then the Brazilian real is likely to gain," the dealer says. That, in turn, would probably bring government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the unwanted appreciation as a strong real hurts exporters and manufacturers. The dealer says \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come in the form of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of dollars from the market "or more drastic measures, such as new taxes on dollar inflows." (rogerio.jelmayer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 6:40 (Dow Jones) More upbeat news for investors of Wyndham (WYN) as the hotel and timeshare operator reported a surprise increase in 4Q EPS amid the company's still-robust stock-buyback efforts while offering a strong 2012 forecast and announcing a 53% surge in the quarterly dividend. Some analysts of late have lauded WYN for being a cash-generating machine and speculated how the company might keep returning it to investors. It spent $225M on buybacks in 4Q and $902M for the year as free cash flow jumped 1/4 in 2011 to $754M. Unlike many companies, WYN has been making well-timed stock purchases, with its average price paid well below current levels, which are at the highest since the 2006 breakup of Cendant. Shares are inactive premarket. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 6:23 (Dow Jones) US stock-index futures are slightly higher as many investors continue to hope for a positive resolution to Greece's debt talks and austerity push. But David Morrison at GFT says, "Further cuts in spending will only exacerbate current troubles. Traders should bear this in mind once any agreement is announced." Today is another one for the US without notable economic data while the morning's quarterly reports from major corporations include CVS, \uc2 Time Warner\uc2  (TWX) and Ralph Lauren (RL). Dow-industrial futures rise 20 points while the S&P 500 tacks on 0.5. (michele.maatouk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-08-12 0646ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120208e82800037\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
