\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Brazil Real May See Little Support Beyond 1.7/USD\b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2012\par 12:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 6:49 (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ) The external backdrop is unlikely to support appreciation of Brazil's real way beyond 1.7/USD short term, at least not until Greece's debt negotiations are resolved, says Santander Economico. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  slows the appreciation trend, but "generally had a limited impact over the medium term," firm says. Around the 1.9-2.0 level, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  starts to become quite nervous about a disorderly move in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and its impact on inflation expectations; in contrast, the government has shown great aversion to sharp strengthening moves in the BRL, Santander Economico says, noting BRL's unlikely to break out from the 1.7-1.9 range. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2181 or email john.shipman@dowjones.com [ 02-07-12 0649ET ]\par \par \uc2 80000   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120207e8270003a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
