\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  c.bank acts to stop  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  rally\b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2012\par 14:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  for first time in 2012\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real gives up gains after auction\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds details, context)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday for the first time in 2012, buying dollar forwards in a bid to curb a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally and keep local manufacturers competitive in a harsh global environment.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, gave up gains immediately after the auction was announced and traded 0.3 percent weaker at 1.7271 reais to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 It underperformed other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as Mexico's peso, which reacted positevely to strong U.S. employment data.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real has gained 8 percent this year as a net 6.5 billion dollars poured into the country in first four weeks of 2012.\par \par \uc2 Analysts were expecting government attempts to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, according to a Reuters poll. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to remain nearly its current levels by the next 12 months, showed the median forecast of 32 strategists surveyed by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was on Dec. 15, when it tried to sell dollars on the spot market.\par \par \uc2 The last dollar forward auction took place on July 26, one day before Brazil's government unveiled a 1-percent tax on derivatives used to bet that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would strengthen.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set a cut-off rate of 1.7383 reais per dollar, and the forwards will settle on March 20.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Silvio Cascione and Jos\u233\'00\'E9 de Castro Editing by W Simon)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2   (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120206e8230010d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
