\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Rally After Strong US Jobs Data\b0\par\par\uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2012\par 21:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , debt rally\par \par \uc2 -- Mexican peso, South African rand hit multi-month highs\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Erin McCarthy \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--An overwhelmingly strong U.S. job reports triggered a rally for emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and debt Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data Friday showed U.S. non-farm payrolls rose by 243,000 in January, nearly double the 125,000 increase expected. The positive surprise gives a boost to expectations for the U.S. economic recovery, which has cheered markets and also provided some support for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  linked to growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The news sent emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a tear, with several hitting fresh multi-month highs, including the Mexican peso, Turkish lira and South African. The Brazilian real also managed to strengthen, despite measures from Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier Friday to weaken the real.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Generally speaking if the U.S. is doing well, almost all emerging markets do well," said Sara Zervos, head of the global debt team and portfolio manager at OppenheimerFunds. "The bulk of emerging markets have a link to the U.S. economy whether it's through exports, commodity demand, [or] U.S. consumer demand."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging market debt also firmed up, as the risk premium on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, or Embig, shrank by 16 basis points to 385 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, its index rose 0.1%. Latin American sovereign debt outperformed, with Venezuela leading the way. Venezuela, whose debt often outpaces wider market swings, saw its spread tighten 45 basis points to 1084 basis points over Treasurys, and its index shot up 1.4%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also were top gainers, particularly the Mexican peso. The peso strengthened to its strongest levels since Sept. 9 against the dollar, which slid about 1% on the day to MXN12.6778, according to CQG. The peso typically reacts positively to solid U.S. economic data, given Mexico's close economic ties to its northern neighbor. Mexico sends about 70% of its exports to the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian real edged up 0.2% against the dollar late Friday, even though Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets early Friday to curb the real's gains for the first time in five months. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held an auction to buy dollars in forward contracts, for delivery March 20, at a rate of BRL1.7383 Brazilian reais. On the Embig, Brazil's spread narrowed by 14 basis points to 205 basis points over Treasurys.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other growth-sensitive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also outperformed. The South African rand strengthened 1.5% against the dollar to its strongest since September 2011, while the Turkish lira also hit a five-month high against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier Friday, Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left its key policy rates unchanged, as expected, saying that current levels will strike the right balance between risks to growth and rising consumer prices for the next few months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Russian ruble only gained modestly against the dollar, which slipped to RUB30.137 from RUB30.197 late Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com @djfxtrader\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Ira Iosebashvili, Paulo Winterstein and Paul Kiernan contributed to this article. [ 03-02-12 2023GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120203e823001cz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
