\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: For  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real, US Data Trumps  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2012\par 15:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 9:51 (Dow Jones) The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's auction to buy dollars for forward delivery ends up having scant effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  marker as the real jumps 1.72/dollar from BRL1.7409 early Friday, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in months to weaken the real was quickly outshined by the release of much-better-than-expected US jobs data. (paul.kiernan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:49 (Dow Jones) It took a little more than two weeks, but the Nasdaq Composite has followed the Nasdaq 100 to 11 year highs. The Comp hit an intraday high of 2889.03, above the May 2, 2011 high of 2887.75, to reach the highest level seen since Jan. 24, 2001. At that high, the index was up 11% so far this year, and 26% from the Oct. 4, 2011 intraday low. The Comp now up 28 at 2888. The Nasdaq 100 first reached an 11-year high on Jan. 19. It's now up 0.8% at 2516, on track for the highest close since Feb. 1, 2001. (tomi.kilgore@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:48 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Walgreen\uc2  exec (WAG) \uc2 Kermit Crawford\uc2  tells Dow Jones that flu shots administered so far this season are below company estimates amid "one of the mildest flu seasons we've seen in a while." The company, the second-largest provider for flu immunizations after the US government, is also being squeezed on the front-end as fewer people are buying over-the-counter medications to treat cough, cold and flu. While January's same-store sales decline was greater than analysts feared, Crawford notes the front-end increase of 1.6% easily bested Wall Street's 0.3% growth projection. (john.kell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:45 (Dow Jones) There's some comfort for Treasury bulls from today's jobs report. The 0.10-percentage-point rise in 10-year yields today only brings it back to the week's high. Jason Rogan at \uc2 Guggenheim Partners\uc2  says the Treasury market is not selling off as much as one might have expected as some are suggesting the strong weather of January might have helped the employment number. In addition, "the Fed comments from last week are helping keep yields from really gapping higher, especially in short-dated Treasurys." Indeed, the 2-year note's yield remains flat at 0.234%, well-anchored by the Fed's decision last week. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:44 (Dow Jones) US mall landlords that operate lower-quality malls will have a tougher time filling vacant space left by expected Sears (SHLD) store closures, Macquarie says. Mall REITs with the biggest exposure to Sears include Rouse Properties (RSE), Pennsylvania REIT (PEI), \uc2 CBL & Associates\uc2  (CBL) and \uc2 Glimcher Realty\uc2  (GRT). Sears stores account for 10%-16% of their square footage in mostly second-tier properties. "If Sears left an already weak mall, there aren't many lower price point tenants that are available, that aren't already in the market or that particular mall," firm says. "There are only so many \uc2 Kohl's\uc2 , JCPenny's or Targets that can be used to re-tenant the space." (angela.pruitt@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:40 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Sunoco\uc2  (SUN) shares up modestly as investors digest the plethora of news the company dropped late Thursday. The 33% dividend increase and 20% share buyback were nice sweeteners, but analysts are also impressed that SUN is closer to becoming something more akin to a profitable MLP than a money-losing refining company. As CEO \uc2 Lynn Elsenhans\uc2  prepares to step down, SUN will keep its pipeline and logistics business while completing the shutdown of its refineries this summer. "Management turned long-blowing winds of change into tailwinds, and are well positioned going into 2012," Tudor Pickering says. SUN up 0.7% at $38.46. (ben.lefebvre@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:35 (Dow Jones) Research In Motion's (RIMM) new CEO has started wooing analysts on Wall Street and Bay Street. Early reviews, contained in this morning's batch of research, are mixed. Macquarie pegs Thorsten Heins as a process guy, "which is important," but say he needs to be paired quickly with a strong, creative chief marketer. National Bank worries BB10 will miss the 2012 holiday season. Neither upgrades their view on the stock. Macquarie is still neutral, and National rates the stock underperform. (chip.cummins@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 9:28 (Dow Jones) Luiz Carlos Baldan, a director at Sao Paulo's Fourtrade brokerage, characterized the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forward auction to buy US dollars auction as a "thermometer." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the real on a near-daily basis during 1H 2011 but has been absent from the market since the European debt crisis escalated around August. "[The bank] decided to do this auction to see how demand would be," Baldan said, adding that he sees the government aiming to keep the real between BRL1.75 and BRL1.85 this year. "It's premature to say that this is the first step in a series of measures." paul.kiernan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 9:26 (Dow Jones) The discount that investors face when using mortgage bonds and other structured debt as collateral for borrowing has declined to 5% from 8% in mid-August, marking a gradual improvement risk-appetite for the sector and overall credit conditions, Fitch Ratings said in a report. Structured debt has increased as a percentage of all repo collateral faster than riskier collateral in aggregate, which also includes corporate bonds and equities, firm said. (albert.yoon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:25 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Urban Outfitters\uc2  (URBN) up 4.4% to $27.60 premarket after Janney boosts shares to buy from neutral, citing leadership changes it expects will help business in 2H, a focus on improving inventory discipline, and improved merchandising at namesake and Anthropologie stores. "We continue to believe in the differentiation of URBN's brands and the loyalty of their customer base," firm says. While shares may be rangebound over the next couple of "transitional quarters," firm recommends accumulation of shares at current levels, and more aggressive buying in the mid-$20 range, and below, should the stock pull back. (karen.talley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:25 (Dow Jones) Don't get hung up on the excess supplies hanging over fertilizer prices, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  says. Expects "a big US spring application season will sop up" the inventory, adds that near-term upside for corn prices will further boost prospects for Mosaic (MOS) and \uc2 CF Industries\uc2  (CF). MOS on Friday became the latest potash company to announce production cuts. But Goldman says investor sentiment should improve next week with a big industry conference possibly sparking new deals and a USDA report boosting crop prices. MOS down 0.1% to $57.03 a share, CF up 1.7% to $185.36 premarket. (ian.berry@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:24 (Dow Jones) So-called \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars are back, says Neal Shearing at London's Capital Economics. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after 5 months of leaving the real be, bought dollars in a forward auction Friday amid concerns its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is getting too strong--again. "Brazilian economic data is improving, but the industrial sector is suffering heavily because of the appreciation of the real. Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now bolsters the case for a rate cut, but I doubt we'll see any capital controls this time." (paul.kiernan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-03-12 0951ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120203e823000a9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
