\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Strengthen After US Jobs Report\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2012\par 14:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared Friday after a key U.S. jobs report showed robust signs of the U.S. economy's recovery.\par \par \uc2 The South African rand and Turkish lira surged to fresh session highs against the dollar, while the Polish zloty rose to its strongest levels of the session against the euro. U.S. nonfarm payrolls rose by 243,000 in January, nearly double the 125,000 increased expected.\par \par \uc2 The overwhelmingly positive surprise gives a boost to expectations for the U.S. economic recovery, which has cheered markets and also provided some support for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  linked to growth.\par \par \uc2 The dollar slid to TRY1.7464 from TRY1.7560 shortly before the jobs data, while the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to ZAR7.5446 against the South African rand from ZAR7.6146 just before the report, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the Polish zloty also shot to session highs.\par \par \uc2 -By Erin McCarthy, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com @djfxtrader [ 02-03-12 0850ET ]\par \par \uc2 -- Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally after U.S. jobs data\par \par \uc2 -- Several \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit fresh multi-month highs\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real weakens on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Updates with additional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most recent levels and investor comments.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened Friday after a key U.S. jobs report showed robust signs of the U.S. economy's recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South African rand strengthened more than 1% against the dollar to its strongest since September 2011, while the Turkish lira also surged to a five-month high against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Data Friday showed U.S. non-farm payrolls rose by 243,000 in January, nearly double the 125,000 increase expected.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The overwhelmingly positive surprise gives a boost to expectations for the U.S. economic recovery, which has cheered markets and also provided some support for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  linked to growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Generally speaking if the U.S. is doing well, almost all emerging markets do well," said Sara Zervos, a senior portfolio manager at Oppenheimer Funds, referring to most emerging markets' trade links to the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar weakened against the Turkish lira to buy as little as TRY1.7464, from TRY1.7574 late Thursday, according to CQG. The lira later pared some of those gains, however. The Czech koruna also advanced, to its strongest since Nov. 7 against the euro. The common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell below the key CZK25 level Friday, most recently trading at CZK24.983.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish zloty strengthened to fresh five-month highs against the euro, which was down 0.3% at PLN4.1768 most recently.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that serve as more prominent proxies for risk also gained on the day. The South African rand climbed more than 1% against the dollar, which changed hands at ZAR1.7554. The Mexican peso, which is seen as the emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that is most tied to the U.S. economy, strengthened 0.6% against the dollar to trade at its strongest levels since last September.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian real, however, wasn't able to join in the U.S.-inspired rally, since Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets early Friday to curb the real's gains for the first time in five months. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held an auction to buy dollars in forward contracts, for delivery March 20, at a rate of BRL1.7383 Brazilian reais. The dollar rose to BRL1.7244 against the real Friday, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com @djfxtrader\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Paulo Winterstein and Paul Kiernan contributed to this article. [ 02-03-12 1154ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120203e8230005o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
