\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-EMERGING MARKETS-Chile peso rallies on China premier comments\b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2012\par 17:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chilean Peso at its strongest in more than 4 months\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  Real firms 0.58 pct, raises \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears\par \par \uc2 * Possible Chinese help to Europe improves global outlook\par \par \uc2 (Updates with new prices for Chile, Mexico, Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Anthony Esposito and Alonso Soto\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO/BRASILIA, Feb 2 (Reuters) - The Chilean peso\par \par \uc2 ended at its strongest level in four and a half months on Thursday, leading a broad strengthening of Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a top official said China may take a bigger role in helping debt-stricken Europe.\par \par \uc2 World markets gained ground after Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said China is "considering increasing its participation in the solution of the European debt crisis" through the region's bailout fund.\par \par \uc2 Rising expectations that Europe will solve its debt crisis as well as Wednesday's upbeat global manufacturing data also helped boost sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were among the best performing in emerging markets in January, after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  calmed fears of a full-blown euro crisis by pumping 489 billion euros of cheap three-year loans into the banking system. [ID: nL2E8D1EI3]\par \par \uc2 "It's partly generation of expectations," said Hernan Jimenez, analyst with \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile in Santiago. "(China's) signal that it could increase (its participation in) the European rescue fund generates... bigger expectations for investors to look for new investment alternatives, perhaps seeking more risk, like in the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Investors tend to dump emerging market assets and buy safe-haven assets like the U.S. dollar to protect themselves against the risk of a deeper economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 "Those comments from China have helped ease market worries ... It adds to this broader optimism that the world economy is improving," said Reginaldo Galhardo, exchange trade manager for Treviso Corretora in Sao Paulo. "This optimism is bringing investors back to emerging markets."\par \par \uc2 A drop in new claims for unemployment benefits in the United States also added strength to the Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso, which was also boosted by stop-loss orders after mining companies, pension funds and banks sold dollars, led the way, closing 1.4 percent firmer to bid 479.90 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso firmed 0.46 percent to 12.83 per dollar, pulling back slightly after hitting its strongest level since mid-September at 12.7850 during the session.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real traded firmer, gaining 0.58 percent to bid 1.7233 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 A stronger real in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised expectations of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has strengthened 8 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 A stronger real lifts the costs for Brazilian producers struggling with a flood a cheaper imports from China.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian Finance Minister Guido Mantega said last week the appreciation was due to dollar weakness abroad, not speculation. However, government officials have said authorities are ready to take actions if the real continues strengthening.\par \par \uc2 Treviso's Galhardo said the market is testing the 1.70 barrier.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Anthony Esposito in Santiago and Alonso Soto in Brasilia; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120205e822000i6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
