\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Ekes Out Small Gain Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2012\par 19:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real exits active trading at BRL1.7471 vs BRL1.7483 Monday\par \par \uc2 --Stronger real so far in 2012 could bring government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --Foreign investors putting money into both stocks and fixed income\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Tom Murphy \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 )--The Brazilian real eked out a tiny gain against the U.S. dollar Tuesday despite renewed worries about possible government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real ended regular trading at BRL1.7471 to the dollar, slightly stronger than the Monday close of BRL1.7483, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian real has gained 7% against the U.S. dollar so far in 2012, once again raising the specter of possible government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In comments earlier this year, Finance Minister Guido Mantega said the government was determined to avoid an "excessive appreciation" of the real against the dollar. He specifically said the government wouldn't allow the real to strengthen to BRL1.60 to the dollar. The strong real hurts exporters and manufacturers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As the real approaches BRL1.70 to the dollar, expectations for government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  begin to rise and the real backs away a little," said Mauriciano Cavalcanti, a trader at Sao Paulo's Ouro Minas brokerage. The real strengthened to BRL1.7350 early Tuesday, before giving up most of its gains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a research note to clients Tuesday, Swiss bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  said government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in the form of dollar purchases from the market or new taxes on investment inflows, could be imminent. "We see the potential for new official measures to curb BRL strength on the horizon," wrote \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Andre Carvalho.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real's strength so far in 2012 has been due, in part, to continued inflows of foreign investment dollars seeking high returns from Brazilian fixed-income investments and stocks. Brazil's Selic base interest rate is high, at 10.5%. Brazil's benchmark Ibovespa stocks index has gained 10% so far this year, making it an attractive investment as well.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could target stocks this time if there are new taxes," said Cavalcanti.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last year, Brazil's government raised taxes on fixed-income inflows from abroad as well as short-term loans and some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives investments. Many foreign investors this year have preferred Brazilian stocks to fixed-income investments on expectations that the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will cut interest rates in the months ahead.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts noted that trading was a bit more volatile Tuesday than normal ahead of monthly expiry Wednesday of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  futures contracts. The contracts will close out based on the average \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate, or Ptax rate, in Tuesday's trading.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Murphy, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 55-11-3544-07090; brazil@dowjones.com [ 31-01-12 1856GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120131e81v001j1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
