\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Weakens On Rate Outlook, Possible  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2012\par 19:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--The Brazilian real weakened slightly on Friday, slipping against the dollar on the outlook that aggressive interest rate cuts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will reduce demand for the Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on concern the government will once again be active in halting the real's gain.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL1.7400 to the dollar, somewhat weaker than its previous close at BRL1.7395, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 The real surged Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there was an "elevated probability" that the Selic rate will move "toward single-digit levels" from its current level of 10.5%.\par \par \uc2 The real jumped more than 1% Thursday on the outlook the rate cuts would spur growth in an economy that has already seen vibrant interest for stocks and bonds; more than $4.8 billion in bonds were issued during the first three weeks of January alone.\par \par \uc2 But the lower rates curb demand for fixed-income investments, a favorite vehicle for overseas investors who borrow developed market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at extremely low rates to buy assets linked to interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The real weakened on Friday after the U.S. reported economic growth of 2.8% during the fourth quarter. Though that represents a faster pace than seen in previous quarters, it still managed to miss market expectations of 3% growth.\par \par \uc2 "Our sense is that a more vocally dovish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a potentially more fragile external environment may take a toll on the BRL," \uc2 Banco Santander\uc2  economists wrote in a Friday note.\par \par \uc2 Traders on Friday also were pocketing some of the previous day's gains in the real on the possibility that the government will step up activity to curb the real's strength.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Guido Mantega earlier this week said that the government will "continue with our policy of preventing the appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the policy of trade defense."\par \par \uc2 The real opened the year at close to BRL1.87 to the dollar and has been strengthening since.\par \par \uc2 "People have been a bit cautious as they await moves by the government or the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 -By Paulo Winterstein, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 55-11-3544-7073; paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com [ 27-01-12 1858GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120127e81r0014l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
