\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Posts Strongest Close In Two Months\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2012\par 20:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil's real closes at strongest level in more than two months\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settles at BRL1.7605 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 --Appreciation has prompted speculation about possible government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Paul Kiernan \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real gained steam in Friday's session to settle at its strongest level against the dollar in more than two months, prompting speculation about the possibility of renewed government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL1.7605 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with Thursday's close of BRL1.7650. Friday's close was the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's best mark against the dollar since early November.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emboldening investors was favorable news from Greece, the country at the heart of the euro zone's debt crisis. A week after talks between the debt-strapped Mediterranean country and its creditors broke down, the two sides on Friday approached a deal to write down 50% of the face value of Greece's debt by exchanging existing bonds for new ones bearing longer maturities and lower interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks posted modest gains while the euro weakened after a week of steadily rising in value against the dollar. Both assets are key barometers of global market sentiment, which frequently sways emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the real.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real has appreciated steadily since ending 2011 at BRL1.8642, spurring talk among market participants about whether local authorities may soon \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . A strong local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  puts \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's exporters and industry at a disadvantage.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think that, when it breaks BRL1.70, they'll have an obligation to enter the market," said Durval Correa, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at Sao Paulo's Multi Money brokerage.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Until shockwaves from the European debt crisis sent the real's value spiraling downward against the dollar around September, Brazil's Finance Ministry and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent much of last year devising ways to keep the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from strengthening too quickly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The measures included taxes on things such as foreign investment in fixed-income securities and higher reserve requirements on banks' short-dollar positions. In addition, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought billions of dollars in spot auctions on the local market, and also auctioned reverse-swap contracts to effectively remove bets against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The tendency, if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't quickly get in with auctions and exchange swaps, is for the exchange rate to fall," Correa said. "There's a lot of investment. With people investing in bonds and stocks, money is quickly coming in and the supply naturally knocks down the dollar's value."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Local media have reported in recent days that authorities are growing uncomfortable with the real's path.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Banco Itau, Brazil's largest private bank, said it is "too early to think seriously about concrete actions" by the government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Tough talking is always the first line of defense," the bank said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Paul Kiernan, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 55-11-3544-7074; paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 20-01-12 1915GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120120e81k000zk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
