\par\par \uc2 Top Stories\par \b \uc2 Brazilian Companies Look Overseas To Escape Volatile Real\b0\par\par\uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2012\par 21:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top News & Commentary\par \uc2 DJCOMM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--A strong real spurred \uc2 Kepler Weber\uc2  (KEPL3.BR) to manufacture grain storage products outside of Brazil last year. They're not expecting another spike in 2012, but have no plans to reverse their decision.\par \par \uc2 In 2011, when the real traded against the dollar at its peak of BRL1.53 in July, the company hired a company in Egypt to manufacture the structures for steel silos, grain dryers and grain cleaning machines for a client there.\par \par \uc2 The move makes the company less vulnerable to swings in the real, because more of its costs and revenue come from outside Brazil. \uc2 Kepler Weber\uc2  plans to conduct more manufacturing overseas, even as the real has weakened in recent months, Collas said.\par \par \uc2 Kepler Weber\uc2  isn't alone. While Brazil's exports rose 27% in 2011, the share from manufactured goods fell to 36.1%, from 39.4% a year earlier. Manufacturers have been gradually moving out of Brazil for years as the cost of doing business in the country has risen, with the strengthening real a major factor.\par \par \uc2 The pressure to leave Brazil is only likely to get worse for the country's exporters. Analysts don't expect the real to immediately return to last year's heights, but see a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the long run. A strong real raises production costs within Brazil, and makes exports more expensive for buyers using other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "For manufacturing companies, it's hard to export from Brazil," says Oscar Becker , CFO at Iochpe-Maxion S.A . (IOCJY), a Brazilian manufacturer of auto parts and railroad cars. \uc2 Iochpe-Maxion\uc2  increasingly relies on its factories overseas to supply foreign buyers, while its Brazilian production meets local demand.\par \par \uc2 Becker expects the real to trade mainly in the range of BRL1.75 to BRL1.80 in 2012. The real traded Thursday at BRL1.8389 to the dollar, 20% below its July peak.\par \par \uc2 Like many emerging markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently to slow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. That marked a sharp reversal from earlier in 2011, when the government enacted a tax on some \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading to curb a surging real. The Brazilian government has also announced it is studying new incentives for local industries to halt the slide in manufacturing export.\par \par \uc2 "Brazil has been losing competitiveness for the last 10 to 12 years. This is a structural problem," said Paulo Vieira da Cunha, a former director at \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a partner in the investment company Tandem Global Partners. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  valuation adds an extra layer to the problem, he said.\par \par \uc2 But even a weaker real won't necessarily reverse some companies' move out of Brazil. They think that even if the real stays far below its 2011 peak this year, it's only a matter of time before the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surges again. Relocating factories and personnel also takes large amounts of time and money, making the decision to head overseas difficult to reverse.\par \par \uc2 It's not just manufacturing that's leaving Brazil. \uc2 JBS S/A\uc2  (JBSAY), the world's largest meat-packing company, in 2011 began taking out loans in U.S. dollars and paying off debt priced in reais. As with exports, a stronger real raises the cost of financing loans compared with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The current program, also motivated by tax savings, involves the transfer of around $2 billion, and could be expanded, said Jeremiah O'Callaghan, JBS's investor relations officer.\par \par \uc2 "We want to have our debt in areas where it is cheaper," he said, adding that he expects the real to trade between BRL1.80 and BRL1.90 this year.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian companies not expanding international \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are still seeking protection from the fluctuating real. A study by research firm Instituto Assaf found an average growth of 21% in the number of future contracts opened at Brazil's BM&FBovespa between 2009 and 2011.\par \par \uc2 Most of that growth reflects a need for protection from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, rather than speculation, said Fabiano Guasti Lima, a researcher at Instituto Assaf.\par \par \uc2 "Brazilian companies are increasingly setting up mechanisms to reduce risk," Lima said.\par \par \uc2 -By Luciana Magalhaes, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2856; luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com;\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 05, 2012 15:22 ET (20:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCOMM1120120105e815003cz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
