\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Slightly Stronger Friday, But Still Weaker For 2011\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2011\par 19:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil real exits active trading at BRL1.8625 Friday, versus BRL1.8664 Thursday\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  posts 11% depreciation against dollar in 2011\par \par \uc2 --Real could rebound in 2012 on rising multinational investments\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Tom Murphy \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real strengthened slightly against the U.S. dollar Friday in thin trading, but still accumulated significant 2011 losses because of international uncertainties.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real ended regular trading at BRL1.8625 to the dollar, slightly stronger than the Thursday close of BRL1.8664, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's financial exchanges were closed Friday as part of year-end holiday celebrations. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading was limited to the interbank market, with small and midcap banks buying the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to build up year-end dollar reserves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real suffered significant losses in the second half of 2011 as worries over a global slowdown and a spreading European debt crisis brought a surge of interest in safe-haven U.S. dollar investments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At midyear, the real traded at its 2011 peak of BRL1.53 to the dollar, but the global worries brought a swift depreciation of the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the U.S. dollar. The 2011 trough for the real was reached in September at BRL1.90 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For 2011 as a whole, the real posted a depreciation of 11% against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For 2012, analysts are looking at continued volatility early in the year but with improving prospects for the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market will open 2012 in a jittery mood, said Paulo Faria-Tavares, managing partner at Sao Paulo's PTX Lending consultants. "There are no foreseeable solutions for Europe," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Guilherme Monaco, a trader at the Hencorp Commcor brokerage in Sao Paulo, said, "The real could reach BRL1.90 to the dollar again on European worries, but that would bring Brazilian government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as in the past."\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in September, selling dollars in order to avoid what officials called "a disorderly market."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, they may have also had another motive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Brazilian real at BRL2.00 to the dollar is not good for inflation," said Monaco.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazilian inflation is at a worrisome 6.6%, with the government pledging to pull it down to 4.5% by early 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the longer term, the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may find some sources of strength against the U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another trader, Olvidio Soares of Sao Paulo's Interbolsa brokerage, said, "The European crisis is very deep. It has been long in the making and it will take years to resolve. However, I believe Europe will soon be able to signal markets that it is at least on the path to solving its problems. At that point, markets will become less volatile."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to Soares, the real could gain against the dollar later in 2012 on continued foreign interest in direct investment in Latin America's biggest economy. "Multinational companies know they have to be here," he said. "Also, investments will pour in ahead of the 2014 World Soccer Cup." The games will be hosted by a dozen Brazilian cities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Soares said the real could strengthen to a range of BRL1.65 to BRL1.70 to the dollar by the end of 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the weekly market survey released by the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , economists predicted a year-end 2012 value for the real of BRL1.75 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3544-07090; brazil@dowjones.com [ 30-12-11 1818GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111230e7cu000kf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
