\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  To Defend BRL1.93-1.95 -RBS\b0\par\par\uc2 163 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2011\par 13:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 7:42 (Dow Jones) Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks set to defend the real whenever it weakens towards BRL1.93-1.95/dollar, predicts RBS. It says, "A proactive stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and willingness shown to provide liquidity could help cap USD/BRL at current levels especially considering the ample \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tools" the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government have. RBS contends that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain focused in the futures market via swaps to mitigate the impact of the IOF tax on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives, which has dried up trading volumes. "Only in the case of disorderly flows would we expect the government to change the regulation on the IOF taxes while dollar sales in spot seem for now still a long way out." (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com [ 10-04-11 0742ET ]\par \par \uc2 1085 80000   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020111004e7a40003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
