\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Stable As  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Eases Volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 By Diana Kinch   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2011\par 23:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed virtually stable against the U.S. dollar Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold exchange-rate swaps to ease some of the downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  caused by the turbulence in international markets.\par \par \uc2 The real exited trading at BRL1.8887 to the dollar, little changed from Monday's close at BRL1.8864, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Despite the stable close, trading was volatile amid nervousness after Greece's worsening debt problems hit global market sentiment and heightened risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 Global markets showed losses early in the day, after news that there would be a delay in new loan aid worth EUR8 billion to Greece due to the canceling of a European ministers' meeting that was expected to consider the issue on Oct. 13. Greek Finance Minister Evangelos Venizelos added to the panic by revealing that Greece has sufficient funds to honor its financial commitments only until mid-November.\par \par \uc2 Greece revealed Monday it's unlikely to meet its fiscal deficit targets for 2011 and 2012 unless revenue collection improves significantly.\par \par \uc2 Shares of European banks fell sharply amid the negative news that could spell significant problems for some financial institutions. Still in the euro zone, factory-gate product prices fell in August due to lower energy costs. Oil and metals fell significantly on international markets while the euro remained volatile.\par \par \uc2 The negative sentiment was aggravated by \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 's downgrading of its global growth domestic product growth forecasts for 2012 to 3.5% from the previous 4.2%, mainly on Europe-related factors.\par \par \uc2 For Brazil, the merchant bank foresees 2011 GDP growth falling to 3.5% from the previously forecast 3.7%, with 2012 growth at 3.3% from the previously forecast 3.8%.\par \par \uc2 Reinforcing the lower expectations, Brazil's statistics bureau announced that industrial production in August fell 0.2% from July, while many economists expected an increase.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold Tuesday 36.6% of the $4.5 billion on offer in four swap contracts, equivalent to just over $1.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also stepped into the fray, selling $1.7 billion in a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts auction to help shore up the real.\par \par \uc2 The auctions offer investors the opportunity to exchange contracts indexed to domestic interest rates for paper linked to the U.S. dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds such auctions when dollars are relatively scarce, causing the depreciation of the real.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted correctly," said Sidnei Nehme of NGO Corretora. "It reduced pressure in the derivatives markets. However, there's also demand in the spot market for a sale of dollars, as we now have a negative \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow." Nehme said international companies are taking dollars out of Brazil to bolster cash reserves at their headquarters abroad.\par \par \uc2 Nehme said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to proceed with further swap auctions and possible cash market sales of dollars at auctions in line with market demand. "The market took up only a third of the swaps offered because the sales price was considered a little high," he said.\par \par \uc2 The real has depreciated sharply against the dollar in recent weeks. On Sept. 1, the real was at BRL1.61 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 According to Tendencias Consultoria's Raphael Martello, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  successfully "neutralized" the impact of a worsening international scenario on the real, and will be forced to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It contained a bit of the real's fall. It's hard to foresee how much it will have to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as this depends more on external factors than anything else," Martello said.\par \par \uc2 -By Diana Kinch, Dow Jones Newswires, Tel: 55 21 2586 6086, diana.kinch@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Matthew Cowley contributed to this article. [ 04-10-11 2121GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111004e7a40019w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
