\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  weaken but Brazil cenbank boosts real\b0\par\par\uc2 823 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2011\par 19:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil acts to protect real after nearly 2 pct slide\par \par \uc2 * Brazil swap sale comes as real slips to 1.9160/dollar\par \par \uc2 * Mexico, Chile pesos weaken on European default concern\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds Colombia peso, Peru sol)\par \par \uc2 By Jeb Blount\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Oct 3 (Reuters) - Brazil's real erased early losses of almost 2 percent to post a gain against the U.S. dollar on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts with a nominal value of $1.71 billion on Monday, part of its effort to limit the real's decline against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The contracts are derivatives that mimic the sale of dollars in the futures market and allow investors to buy insurance, or "a hedge," against a weaker real. For details, see [ID:nE5E7JI03V]\par \par \uc2 "This shows that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to act if they see a sharp movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Carlos Kawall, chief economist with Banco Safra in Sao Paulo. " This was more about the speed of today's movement than a specific level."\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> gained 0.56 percent to end at 1.8905 per dollar at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 5 p.m. local time (2000 GMT) close. It earlier weakened as much as 1.88 percent to 1.9160.\par \par \uc2 Some investors have suggested that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's auction showed it is ready to defend the real if it weakens beyond 1.90 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil plans to sell another $4.53 billion of swaps on Tuesday. [ID:nE5E7JI03W]\par \par \uc2 Only months ago, Brazil had been concerned about the real becoming too strong vis-a-vis the dollar. But now it is stepping in to halt the real's decline as concerns about potential European debt defaults and sluggish global growth prompt investors to sell assets in higher-risk emerging markets, such as Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The real, which had touched 12-year highs in late July, has reversed gains to fall nearly 12 percent against the greenback so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Much of the decline has come after Brazil's government in July imposed a 1 percent tax on investors who increase their bets the real will gain.\par \par \uc2 The real has also declined following a decision to cut the country's benchmark interest rate by 50 basis points to 12 percent on Aug. 31.\par \par \uc2 The real may be in for further declines after foreign investors cut their net bets the real will gain to their lowest level in 15 months. [ID:nN1E7920D3]\par \par \uc2 Earlier the real and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on rising concern Greece will not meet the requirements of a debt bailout plan needed to stave off a sovereign debt default.\par \par \uc2 Greek officials said the country will not meet its deficit target for 2011 even as it imposes austerity measures to boost revenue and cut future borrowing needs -- requirements made by the European Union and International Monetary fund before they will lend the country new cash to pay maturing debt. [ID:nL5E7L31G6]\par \par \uc2 Without aid, Greece will likely default, an action that could saddle international banks with huge costs and crimp lending worldwide. At the same time, the U.S. and European economies, responsible for about half of world output, are already showing signs of a slowdown. [ID:nN1E7920VY]\par \par \uc2 If China, the world's second-largest economy also slows, demand for the oil, copper iron-ore and other commodities that are the backbone of Latin America's exports may fall.\par \par \uc2 "All emerging markets are very sensitive to every piece of news that is coming out about Europe's (debt) problem," said Enrique Trejo, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Banorte-Ixe in Mexico City. "There is fear of a recession in Europe and the United States. Investors are looking for less risk."\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=D2> weakened 0.97 percent to 14.0315 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Without a resolution of Europe's debt crisis, which risks spreading from Greece to Spain, Italy and Portugal, Mexico's peso should trade in the 13.78 to 14.10 pesos per dollar range, Trejo said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=CL> shed 1.08 percent to 525.10 to the dollar. Chile is the world's largest producer and exporter of copper, and the price of the metal has plunged in recent weeks to 14-month lows. Copper for delivery in three months <CMCU3> fell 2 percent to $6,876.00 a tonne in London.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's peso <COP2=STFX> fell 1.55 percent to 1,960.30 per dollar while Peru's sol <PEN=PE> lost 0.11 percent to 2.7750, its weakest level since July 7.\par \par \uc2 It may have lost more if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not sold $38 million in the spot market in an attempt to limit the unit's losses.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111006e7a3001a5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
