\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-UPDATE 2-Brazil move to check  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  slide unlikely soon\b0\par\par\uc2 1,065 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2011\par 16:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Real has shed 15 pct since 12-year high in July\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank last bolstered real after 35 pct two-month loss\par \par \uc2 * Brazil more stable, capital flow stronger than 2008-09\par \par \uc2 * Possible Greek default could change \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  outlook\par \par \uc2 * Cen bank not signaling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on swap roll -source\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment on reverse-swap decision)\par \par \uc2 By Silvio Cascione and Jeb Blount\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/RIO DE JANEIRO, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to act soon to limit a slide in the real that has sent the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <BRBY> to its weakest level in 13 months.\par \par \uc2 Capital flows in Brazil are strong, and the economy is more stable than it was when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the real by selling dollars at auction, during the 2008-2009 U.S. banking crisis and world recession.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar sales remain unlikely despite the real's 13.6 percent decline this month, which has helped reverse one of the world's biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains into one of the biggest losses.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost nearly 10 percent year-to-date against the dollar after erasing a nearly 8 percent gain from January though July 26, when the real hit a 12-year high of 1.5275 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 With the real now trading at about 1.85 per dollar, market players speculate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will wait until the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens much further before stepping in to buy the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to support it.\par \par \uc2 Some see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comfortable with the real weakening to 1.90 reais per dollar or others to 2 reais per dollar since this would help manufacturers who have complained that a strong real has dented their competitive edge abroad.\par \par \uc2 "We don't see the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now," said Mario Battistel, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Fair Corretora, a Sao Paulo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage, when asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in to curb the real's slide.\par \par \uc2 "When people say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sell dollars, they imagine that the real is very weak -- when the true consensus is that the real is strong," he said.\par \par \uc2 The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling dollars to halt a plunge in the real was in Oct. 8, 2008, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had lost more than a third of its value in two months and was trading as weak as 2.44 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the real weakened about 3.5 percent in afternoon trading to 1.8566 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 From May 2009 until Sept. 13 this year -- with only short breaks of a day or two -- the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been buying dollars as much as twice a day at auction to limit gains by the real. From its December 2009, post-U.S. crisis lows of 2.619, the real gained over 50 percent through September 2011.\par \par \uc2 The gains had raised the ire of Brazilian manufacturers who felt the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spurring a flood of imports and pricing their products out of foreign markets.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? Quite the contrary. Right now the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be happy with the real at 2 to the dollar," said Andre Ferreira, partner and head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at brokerage Futura Corretora in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 DOLLAR INFLOWS STILL STRONG\par \par \uc2 Current market conditions are also very different than they were in 2008 and 2009, said Arnaldo Puccinelli, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Banif Investment Bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Three years ago the world market was suffering with the bankruptcy of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 , a world-wide recession and the disappearance of interbank credit, which provoked capital flight from emerging markets such as Brazil.\par \par \uc2 A similar scenario is likely now only if a debt crisis in Europe results in a sovereign default. A default in Greece and other European countries could lead to massive banking losses and a restriction of credit that would threaten to choke off world growth. For details, see [ID:nL3E7KK0MS]\par \par \uc2 "If Greece defaults, all bets are off," said Joao Medeiros, a partner at Pioneer Corretora, a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, dollars continue to pour into Brazil. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday that net dollar inflows were $8.52 billion in the first 15 days of September, boosting net flows in the year to more than $68 billion. [ID:nS1E78D0XW]\par \par \uc2 In the opinion of the head of treasury at one of Brazil's dealer banks, one of the 14 authorized to do business directly with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , only a rapid change in the outlook for the country would lead to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the real hits 1.90 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The flows and exchange rate are still OK," he said on the condition of anonymity, citing company policy.\par \par \uc2 If it were to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling dollars, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has plenty of dollars to sell, as recent dollar buys have amassed a record $350 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Alexandre Tombini has mentioned the reserves as one of the main protections Brazil has against international financial crises.\par \par \uc2 A possible intermediate step toward direct dollar sales in the market would be to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the futures market, the dealer bank treasurer said.\par \par \uc2 A principal source of foreign bets on a stronger real in recent months was in the futures market, although much of this long-real position has been undone.\par \par \uc2 About $2 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps come due this month, the treasurer said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could let them expire without selling new swaps.\par \par \uc2 As the sale of the reverse swaps mimics buying dollars, letting them expire, or buying back outstanding reverse swaps early, would help bolster the real without selling reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday that it will not refinance, or "roll-over" the $1.98 billion of reverse swaps coming due Oct. 1.\par \par \uc2 The bank is not signaling plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market with the decision not to refinance the reverse swaps, a member of the Brazilian government's economic team told Reuters.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows to the country remain vigorous and the market is functioning well, the source said. [ID:nS1E78K1LE]\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Isabel Versiani in Brasilia, Editing by Patricia Duarte, W Simon, Leslie Adler )\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS) (UPDATE 2)  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110924e79l000fh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
